{
  "$comment": "Every Javelin message type this client build ships, with its AZ type GUID and the wire type number that actually goes on the wire. Source: a scan of NewWorld.exe for the packed 'XxxMsg' name + dashed-GUID descriptor region, then each GUID resolved to its POSITION in the per-build type table (private-client/runtime/typeindex.json; disk.py copies it from the install). The wire carries the table index, not the GUID, so this table is what turns a message name into bytes. Validated independently: all 12 previously-known movement-family wire types reproduce exactly. A null wire_type means the GUID is registered in the binary but absent from the type table, so it cannot be addressed on the wire. Regenerate on a client update with reverse/tools/scan-message-registry.py.",
  "build_sha256": "8654f01d324636d9f74f1c793b0cc4a417c3c5fa9847d9913c358ca29e0fdc8e",
